WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 7.5 · Brand, Identity & Image
Visual identity

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
A simple visual system used everywhere makes you recognisable, even before your logo is finished.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:28.133
Visual identity is the set of visual elements that makes you recognisable: logo, colours, typefaces, imagery and layout. The system matters more than any single element, and you can start it before the logo is finished.

4
00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:29.133
The core elements

5
00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:41.574
Logo: A main version, a small version, and light and dark versions, with spacing rules. For example: Until the logo is ready, the bakery uses a clean wordmark on its stall banner.

6
00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:52.163
Colour: Two or three main colours and a few supporting ones, with screen and print codes. For example: Warm brown and cream, with dark grey for text.

7
00:00:52.163 --> 00:01:02.011
Type: One or two typefaces that anyone who joins can use, free or licensed. For example: One free typeface for both headings and body text.

8
00:01:02.011 --> 00:01:13.430
Imagery: Honest, respectful images of real people, taken with informed consent. For example: Photos of trainees at work, with their written consent, faces only where agreed.

9
00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:14.430
Why it matters

10
00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:19.733
1. People recognise you faster when everything looks like one family.

11
00:01:19.733 --> 00:01:25.037
2. Accessibility built in now is cheaper than fixing it later.

12
00:01:25.037 --> 00:01:30.230
3. Respectful images protect people and your credibility.

13
00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:31.230
Where it goes

14
00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:36.163
1. Your brand guidelines and templates, in the next lesson.

15
00:01:36.163 --> 00:01:40.356
2. Your website, social profiles, posters and proposals.

16
00:01:40.356 --> 00:01:45.178
3. Your co-branding with partners and funders.

17
00:01:45.578 --> 00:01:46.178
What to avoid

18
00:01:46.178 --> 00:01:51.111
Paying an expensive agency before you know your audiences.

19
00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:56.415
Low contrast, small text or information shown by colour alone.

20
00:01:56.415 --> 00:02:02.719
Stereotyped images, or photos of children without consent and safeguards.

21
00:02:03.319 --> 00:02:05.119
You define the first elements of your visual identity.

22
00:02:05.119 --> 00:02:09.119
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:13.719
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
